      "title": "Polanski says he does not need to win ‘50/50’ byelection to stay Green leader",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/02/polanski-green-leader-authority-byelection-holborn-pancras",
      "description": "<p>Exclusive: Party leader says outcome of ‘knife-edge’ vote in Keir Starmer’s former seat will not affect his position</p><p>Zack Polanski has said his authority as leader of the Green party of England and Wales does not depend on winning next week’s Holborn and St Pancras byelection, amid suggestions the party’s popularity may have peaked.</p><p>Polanski, who is trying to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/07/we-can-win-here-zack-polanski-presses-the-flesh-in-holborn-and-st-pancras\">take Keir Starmer’s former seat</a> from Labour, described the contest as “probably 50/50 right now” and “really on a knife edge”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/02/polanski-green-leader-authority-byelection-holborn-pancras\">Continue reading...</a>",
